  "body": "## The bug (found by the live test)\n\nThe hybrid's \"did the install actually land?\" check read `uv-receipt.toml` and matched `version = \"$Version\"`. The live test showed uv does **not** reliably write that receipt into a recreated tool dir, so the check returned false even though the install succeeded — the installer wrongly threw and rolled back after a successful tool-env update.\n\n## The fix\n\nThe `.dist-info` directory (`my_claude_code-<ver>.dist-info`) exists only if uv actually installed the package into the fresh tool dir. It needs no python to run and is testable with a stub.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Live: after a uv exit-2 on a locked shim, the canonical tool dir's `site-packages` contains `my_claude_code-5.3.4.dist-info`.\n- New locked-shim test stub creates the dist-info dir. All 6 rename tests pass; ruff/ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.3.4 → 5.3.5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
