    "message": "fix(install): detect the fresh install landed via dist-info, not the uv receipt\n\nThe hybrid's \"did the install actually land?\" check read uv-receipt.toml and\nmatched version = \"$Version\". Live test showed uv does NOT reliably write that\nreceipt into a recreated tool dir, so the check returned false even though the\ninstall succeeded -- the installer wrongly threw and rolled back after a\nsuccessful tool-env update. The dist-info directory (my_claude_code-<ver>\n.dist-info) exists only if uv actually installed the package into the fresh\ntool dir, needs no python to run, and is testable with a stub. Uses that.\n\nVerified live: after a uv exit-2 on a locked shim, the canonical tool dir's\nsite-packages contains my_claude_code-5.3.4.dist-info. New locked-shim test\nstub creates the dist-info dir. All 6 rename tests pass; ruff/ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.3.4 -> 5.3.5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
